9d1a|n|A painting on a wall or ceiling; a single piece comprehended in one view, and formed according to one design; hence, a picture in general. ; An ancient mode of indicating musical sounds by letters and other signs instead of by notes. ; Division into plates or tables with intervening spaces; as, the tablature of the cranial bones.	a:ria,133,4;9zn0,129,3;6pto,109,8;2o18,81,2;5z2v,9,3~6pto,109,8;ria,133,4;5z2v,9,3;9zn0,129,3;2o18,81,2	v:6pto,79,1;7ra7,26,3;4emi,25,5;7r3f,25,8;1883,16,3~7r3f,25,8;4emi,25,5;7ra7,26,3;1883,16,3;6pto,79,1	V:4fnq,54,4~4fnq,54,4	n:3wjj,112,58;6pto,79,1;2o18,71,1;90ed,62,3;k8f,61,4;62ho,59,6;6f42,51,5;4yv7,43,3;9cwi,40,4;7ra7,20,2~3wjj,112,58;62ho,59,6;6f42,51,5;9cwi,40,4;k8f,61,4;90ed,62,3;4yv7,43,3;7ra7,20,2;2o18,71,1;6pto,79,1	N:6f42,70,18;8trd,43,8;2rgf,43,3;9cwi,36,3;3f14,31,4~6f42,70,18;8trd,43,8;3f14,31,4;9cwi,36,3;2rgf,43,3
