9efr|n|A gentle or slight blow; a light rap; a pat. ; A piece of leather fastened upon the bottom of a boot or shoe in repairing or renewing the sole or heel. ; A signal, by drum or trumpet, for extinguishing all lights in soldiers' quarters and retiring to bed, -- usually given about a quarter of an hour after tattoo. ; A hole or pipe through which liquor is drawn. ; A plug or spile for stopping a hole pierced in a cask, or the like; a faucet. ; Liquor drawn through a tap; hence, a certain kind or quality of liquor; as, a liquor of the same tap. ; A place where liquor is drawn for drinking; a taproom; a bar. ; A tool for forming an internal screw, as in a nut, consisting of a hardened steel male screw grooved longitudinally so as to have cutting edges.	a:8xky,93,152;a0ej,92,4;b83,89,93;28c2,83,1;2omk,81,3;3mc1,75,4;66z4,75,2;1mo1,73,8;2k88,73,5;3aqt,72,11;89il,72,1;74j2,71,21;3yvr,60,6;5fqs,60,7;9l98,57,4~2m07,51,3084;8pm3,31,1461;16fj,16,451;1d3l,31,409;8egs,6,387;45xr,40,314;1n86,45,255;5dsp,1,208;1d81,47,186;8xky,93,152;7v2v,9,105;b83,89,93;590q,5,93;7ni3,11,92;agbv,42,90	v:a0ej,87,3;28c2,83,1;121d,82,11;1hda,72,8;2omk,65,1;2nlf,63,30;3aqt,61,5;a4fy,49,4;19zr,41,3;9bdm,38,1;aaqv,36,3;9ruz,33,2;13ib,31,35;74ra,30,4;aeam,27,5~2de9,7,45;13ib,31,35;2nlf,63,30;13o7,7,21;55xb,25,15;121d,82,11;1hda,72,8;6oef,12,7;3aqt,61,5;aeam,27,5;14yu,21,4;a4fy,49,4;10t2,22,4;74ra,30,4;a0ej,87,3	V:9eh1,88,13;3qcx,69,6;7sk8,63,6;3rnj,62,3;5zw1,53,2;2nlf,50,12;248e,49,24;au42,46,14;4qwd,45,2;au3h,41,33;7b6j,38,3;3n4x,35,14;3dp,32,9;13p0,31,7;2nk5,25,22~8acl,1,109;2msc,23,82;2dnt,19,82;6k5l,13,59;au3h,41,33;248e,49,24;2nk5,25,22;au42,46,14;3n4x,35,14;9eh1,88,13;9efr,4,12;2nlf,50,12;3dp,32,9;13p0,31,7;3qcx,69,6	n:857n,88,18;1e36,76,2;89il,72,1;37gz,68,75;aa0u,68,4;3c03,61,1;13ib,60,270;3aqo,60,403;9rtr,59,12;8xky,57,13;1k0a,57,4;4vr7,57,29;5vof,55,73;941s,54,9;9ux6,54,3~a6j7,12,996;1d3l,43,933;agmu,36,735;3aqo,60,403;13ib,60,270;16fj,7,248;13o7,41,222;319b,6,214;2dnt,33,206;1d81,47,186;