9fc4|n|A body occurring in small quantity in the juices of muscle, in the lungs, and elsewhere, but especially in the bile, where it is found as a component part of taurocholic acid, from which it can be prepared by decomposition of the acid. It crystallizes in colorless, regular six-sided prisms, and is especially characterized by containing both nitrogen and sulphur, being chemically amido-isethionic acid, C2H7NSO3.	a:5s1m,88,2;9cdp,77,1;9cdf,71,1;2wu8,48,10;6tfq,28,3~2wu8,48,10;6tfq,28,3;5s1m,88,2;9cdp,77,1;9cdf,71,1	v:9cdf,109,14;5ibu,18,5~9cdf,109,14;5ibu,18,5	n:zre,82,6;5s1m,78,1;598y,19,12~598y,19,12;zre,82,6;5s1m,78,1	N:1qoy,113,6;57hm,59,3;1tax,36,4~1qoy,113,6;1tax,36,4;57hm,59,3
